# Real iCE40 (device "384") chipdb — a CELL-TO-CELL routing slice, verbatim from Project IceStorm.
# Generated by `icebox_chipdb.py -3`; every .net/.buffer block below is copied byte-for-byte from the full
# device chipdb. It is a real intra-tile connection on tile (1,1): logic cell 0's output (net 39 =
# lutff_0/out) reaches logic cell 5's input pin 1 (net 1121 = lutff_5/in_1) through the local track
# local_g0_0 (net 1057), via two real buffer pips. This lets fpga-icebox-synth.ts route a real logical net
# from one placed cell to another and assemble the full design's bitstream. The full chipdb is ~2 MB.
#
# icebox is ISC-licensed, Copyright (C) 2015 Claire Xenia Wolf <claire@clairexen.net>:
#   Permission to use, copy, modify, and/or distribute this software for any
#   purpose with or without fee is hereby granted, provided that the above
#   copyright notice and this permission notice appear in all copies.
#
.device 384 8 10 8294
.net 39
0 1 logic_op_rgt_0
0 2 logic_op_bnr_0
1 0 logic_op_top_0
1 1 lutff_0/out
1 2 neigh_op_bot_0
2 0 logic_op_tnl_0
2 1 neigh_op_lft_0
2 2 neigh_op_bnl_0
.net 1057
1 1 local_g0_0
.net 1121
1 1 lutff_5/in_1
.buffer 1 1 1057 B0[14] B1[14] B1[15] B1[16] B1[17]
10001 39
.buffer 1 1 1121 B10[27] B10[28] B10[29] B10[30] B11[30]
00100 1057
